<article class="guide-article">
  <h1>More ideas &amp; prompts</h1>
  <p class="article-date">Companion to <a href="/guides/personal-website-muse-github-pages/">Publish and maintain a personal website using Muse from Meta and GitHub Pages for free</a></p>

  <p>Every entry below is a real idea I had while building this site, the gist of the prompt I gave Muse, and where it landed. Steal the pattern: describe what you want, give an example or two, and let the AI do the typing.</p>

  <div class="ipr-grid">
    <dl class="ipr-card">
      <dt>Idea</dt>
      <dd>A single source of truth for all my projects, with filtering and sorting.</dd>
      <dt>Prompt</dt>
      <dd class="prompt-text">&ldquo;Consolidate my projects into one projects.json data file, newest first. Home shows the 6 newest cards with a &lsquo;View all&rsquo; link, and build a /projects/ page with tag filter chips and Newest/Oldest/A&ndash;Z sorting that works without JS.&rdquo;</dd>
      <dt>Result</dt>
      <dd><a href="/projects/">Projects</a></dd>
    </dl>
    <dl class="ipr-card">
      <dt>Idea</dt>
      <dd>A proper mobile nav that degrades gracefully.</dd>
      <dt>Prompt</dt>
      <dd class="prompt-text">&ldquo;Collapse the header nav into a hamburger menu under 640px that closes on link tap, Escape, or outside tap. With JS disabled the links should just render as a stacked list &mdash; desktop untouched.&rdquo;</dd>
      <dt>Result</dt>
      <dd><a href="/">Home</a> (shrink your browser window to see the mobile menu)</dd>
    </dl>
    <dl class="ipr-card">
      <dt>Idea</dt>
      <dd>Hero copy that captures my personality in wordplay.</dd>
      <dt>Prompt</dt>
      <dd class="prompt-text">&ldquo;Replace my homepage hero copy with my taglines &mdash; the B-line all b-words, the F-line all f-words &mdash; and tighten the spacing underneath.&rdquo;</dd>
      <dt>Result</dt>
      <dd><a href="/">Home</a></dd>
    </dl>
    <dl class="ipr-card">
      <dt>Idea</dt>
      <dd>Never ship a stale CSS/JS file after a push again.</dd>
      <dt>Prompt</dt>
      <dd class="prompt-text">&ldquo;Add cache-busting to my build: append a content-hash ?v= query string to every local CSS and JS URL so browsers always fetch the fresh copy.&rdquo;</dd>
      <dt>Result</dt>
      <dd><a href="/">Home</a> (view source and look for the ?v= hashes)</dd>
    </dl>
    <dl class="ipr-card">
      <dt>Idea</dt>
      <dd>SEO and accessibility baseline across the whole site.</dd>
      <dt>Prompt</dt>
      <dd class="prompt-text">&ldquo;Do the SEO and accessibility quick wins: favicon, OG and Twitter cards, canonical URLs, JSON-LD Person markup, a sitemap.xml, a custom 404 page, a skip-to-content link, and no mixed-content social links.&rdquo;</dd>
      <dt>Result</dt>
      <dd><a href="/">Home</a></dd>
    </dl>
    <dl class="ipr-card">
      <dt>Idea</dt>
      <dd>A minimalist redesign variant &mdash; a single 660px near-monochrome column.</dd>
      <dt>Prompt</dt>
      <dd class="prompt-text">&ldquo;One of the redesign variants should be ultra-minimal: a narrow centered column, near-monochrome palette, system fonts, nothing flashy &mdash; let the content do the work.&rdquo;</dd>
      <dt>Result</dt>
      <dd><a href="/vibe-redesign/minimalist/">Minimalist variant</a></dd>
    </dl>
    <dl class="ipr-card">
      <dt>Idea</dt>
      <dd>A neo-brutalist redesign variant with hard shadows and candy colors.</dd>
      <dt>Prompt</dt>
      <dd class="prompt-text">&ldquo;Make one variant full neo-brutalist: thick black borders, hard offset shadows, candy-bright blocks of color &mdash; loud on purpose.&rdquo;</dd>
      <dt>Result</dt>
      <dd><a href="/vibe-redesign/neubrutalist/">Neo-brutalist variant</a></dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

